      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T18:00:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not clear to me that \u0027Performance \u003c-\u003e Degraded\u0027.  The tires on my car might be considered \"degraded\" if they are near the end of life or they have a air low pressure, but that doesn\u0027t mean they spin less slowly.  Similarly, memory can have degraded ECC capability due to a DRAM chip failure but not have any performance implication.\n\nAre we sure that \"degraded\" from a DMTF perspective is meant to mean \"worse performance\"?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "76dbe283015f918a21d8c644de915457323d8d58",
