        "id": 1002885
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-05T06:20:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The PDI doesn\u0027t define a threshold for this.\n\nFor my implementing service(PLDM), it reflects what the devices or its firmware reports, by using pre-define state set at DSP0249(v1.4.0), Table 1, State Set 14.\n\nRef:\nhttps://www.dmtf.org/sites/default/files/standards/documents/DSP0249_1.4.0.pdf\n\nIn this case, I think the definition of `degraded` is defined by the vendor itself.",
      "parentUuid": "07a8ce9c_326d35d0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "76dbe283015f918a21d8c644de915457323d8d58",
