    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5da5f11_ec096192",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-06T17:02:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Redfish Status::State talks about a function or resource - how do we map Performance to this? How do we know if performance or functionality or the resource itself is degraded?\n\nAlso, DSP0249 has \"degraded\" defined for performance as well as operational status: how do we map to Redfish?",
      "parentUuid": "341cc432_e3ad34ee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "76dbe283015f918a21d8c644de915457323d8d58",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d75d1fe_70611d4a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002885
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-08T05:23:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com,\n\nRegarding the Redfish Status::State issue, I was deducing the mapping through the following logic. `Redfish Status::State` defines several enum properties, including `Degraded` and `Updating`.\n\n```\n\"State\": {\n    \"enumDescriptions\": {\n        ...,\n        \"Degraded\": \"The function or resource is degraded.\",\n        ...,\n        \"Updating\": \"The element is updating and might be unavailable or degraded.\"\n    },\n    \"enumLongDescriptions\": {\n        ..., \n        \"Degraded\": \"This value shall indicate the resource is enabled but operating in a degraded mode.\",\n        ..., \n        \"Updating\": \"This value shall indicate the element is updating.  The element may become unavailable or operate at a degraded level of performance or functionality.\"\n    },\n}\n```\n\nAs of my opinion, `Degraded` and `Updating` are both property of Redfish Status::State, thus they should be indicating same property with different value.\nOn the other hand, `Updating` indicates the element is updating and might be degraded(in short description), and in the long description it has explicitly mentioned \"The element may become unavailable or operate at a degraded level of performance or functionality.\"\n\nI see this as an indirect evidence that Redfish Status::State accepts degraded in either functionality or performance. In this case, I modified in PS9 to move `degraded` property to the existing interface of `OperationalStatus`.\n\nRegarding the second question, as DMTF redfish schema explicitly mentioned degraded indicates either functional or performance aspects degraded, I think both of the PLDM state set should be mapped to the same property then, which means `degraded` is true either performance or functional degraded happened.",
      "parentUuid": "a5da5f11_ec096192",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "76dbe283015f918a21d8c644de915457323d8d58",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
